{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/940856-kupala-the-fertile-god-of-carpathia","id":940856,"title":"Kupala; The Fertile God Of Carpathia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T14:33:01-07:00","id":940856,"title":"Kupala; The Fertile God Of Carpathia","content":"&quot;We stood under the shadow of Dara our coats drenched in sweat from the humid July air, our alpha Reaps-The-Harvest had shifted to Gauru while we waited, she always did this when we made the yearly sacrifice her mastery of the fathers form is admirable to say the least. We lit our bonfire and prepared the a bowl of hearts blood of animals and men hunted during the Siskur-Dah before the fire. Reaps-The-Harvest begun to chant; &quot;On this night we bring our sacrifice of blood to you oh great Kupala great lord of this land we bring this sacrifice of blood to appease you and your brood.&quot; as we bowed our heads a creature emerged from the darkness, a man like shape but made of soil, and rock, and fire. It approached our Alpha as she lifted the now white hot bowl with her talons. The creature took it and sipped from the burning bowl and smiled, it had no teeth but spoke in an other worldly voice &quot;Good we are pleased with this Uthra.&quot; it proceeded to take the bowl and proceed towards Dara intent on taking it to the peak. &quot;Kupala shall be pleased by this&quot; echoed as it began its ascent. Kupala's servant shall stay quiet for the passing of this season, this is the cycle we follow, life, death, rebirth, and blood.&quot;<br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I have been sitting on this fluff for a while now, this is a short paragraph I wrote when had the idea to translate Kupala into Forsaken. I also did this for my World Of Darkness setting in which Forsaken replaces Apocalypse, but never made any actual stats for Kupala as an Earth Bound Spirit. So I ask anyone who is interested in brainstorming ideas for Kupala and his Servants please do comment and let me know what you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:47:51-07:00","id":940929,"title":"","content":"I guess the obvious thing if you wanted to go wild with it would be to have it as an idigam.<br /> <br /> But a more proactive spirit seems the most appropriate for what, admittedly, little I know about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:18:38-07:00","id":941249,"title":"","content":"I'd probably second the idigam option. From what little I've read of Kupala, he sounds like he could fit the bill for one of the Earthbound, those that managed to escape being sent to Luna only to be tied to an extent to interactions with humankind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T12:05:50-07:00","id":941326,"title":"","content":"I would vote for Kupala as Earthbound idigam simply because it would be a shout out for its origin as Earthbound Demon. I think that terraforming abilities should be appropriate for it, considering its connection to Koldun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:16:30-07:00","id":942937,"title":"","content":"Agreed, though in that case, perhaps its Essence Shaping could affect vampires( or at least one that focuses on kindred)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:13:54-07:00","id":943082,"title":"","content":"You could always cleave a little closer to the local real world mythology, but, I can see you're clearly wanting to 'translate' Kupala 1.0' into 'Kupala 2.0', so:<br /> <br /> I would stay away from anything infernal. The Hisil is pretty brutal even <i>without</i> demons. Maybe the Kupala these cultists worship is a highly-specialized Royal Avatar of, say, the spirit of the entire Carpathian Mountains? Maybe it's grown used to blood sacrifice, to the point where it can now only reap Essence from ritualized death...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:38:04-07:00","id":943830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/940856-kupala-the-fertile-god-of-carpathia?p=943082#post943082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always cleave a little closer to the local real world mythology, but, I can see you're clearly wanting to 'translate' Kupala 1.0' into 'Kupala 2.0', so:<br /> <br /> I would stay away from anything infernal. The Hisil is pretty brutal even <i>without</i> demons. Maybe the Kupala these cultists worship is a highly-specialized Royal Avatar of, say, the spirit of the entire Carpathian Mountains? Maybe it's grown used to blood sacrifice, to the point where it can now only reap Essence from ritualized death...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kupala 1.0? What do you mean by that, do you mean old world of darkness? Also I was not going close to demons for this, I think the idea of the Demons being involved is disrespectful. That is why I am doing this, I saw how Kupala was portrayed in Old World of Darkness and did not like it. The whole idea of it being a giant Wyrm Beast was quite annoying and lazy in my opinion. Also very disrespectful to the people who do worship Kupala to this day. I like the idea of the Royal Avatar of the Carpathians that has been there since the formation of the land. But I do not want this to be the nicest god like creature. I want it to be mainly bent on keeping the order of life going. Blood sacrifice quenches its thirst allowing for it to continue on with its purpose. Blood it has grown accustomed to, but the festival of Kupala Night is what also sustains this great god like beast. The Emotions of the people who keep the old tradition going allow it to reap much essence from the night he is held in reverence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}